        version: "0.1.0-build.126",
        tag: "v0.1.0-build.126",
        date: "2026-08-04T01:08:00-04:00",
        commit: "fc084e8b8d17e86bf3c082de208f9e5d36e168b2",
        entries: [
            {
                sha: "fc084e8b8d17e86bf3c082de208f9e5d36e168b2",
                shortSha: "fc084e8b8d",
                date: "2026-08-04T01:08:00-04:00",
                subject: "Give the app a palette, a notice history, a changelog, and a builder on every search",
                details: "Four contracts, built in parallel and wired here.\n\nThe command palette is one shortcut over every command, setting and\ndestination: 30 rows assembled from the registries that already exist,\nso a sixth settings section or an eighth config tab appears in it on\nthe same commit that adds it rather than when somebody remembers. A\nrow that is a setting renders the real control and writes through the\nsame path the settings page uses; a row that is a destination says\nwhere it goes and gets there through the shell's existing reveal, not\na second one. It defaults to the bounded card, because a search box\nthat swallows the window is worse than one you opted into.\n\nThe notification bell was already in the corner and was very nearly\ndecorative: a count over a flat list with no search and no way back.\nIt is a real centre now, and the contract around it stopped being an\nintention: one test asserts every level lands as a corner toast with\nno dialog anywhere in the document and that warnings outlive an hour\nwhile info dismisses at five seconds, and another inventories every\ndialog in the package and demands each one name the decision it asks\nfor. \"It reports something\" is not an admissible answer, and that test\ncaught a palette added minutes earlier.\n\nThe changelog is generated from the repository rather than written:\n35 versions and 88 entries, each carrying the commit that made it,\nevery SHA validated before anything is written. Versions come from\ntags with `rev-list --not` rather than pairwise ranges, because three\ntags sit on a side branch and a range would have lost them. Categories\ncome from the paths a commit touched, not from its wording, because\nthese commits carry no feat/fix marker and a label inferred from prose\nis a changelog saying what nobody wrote. CI now fails when it drifts.\n\nThe regex builder reached four collections that had no search at all -\nrelease assets, downloads, interrupted renders and the wizard's review\nlists - and the profiles list, which is the one that grows without\nanybody deciding it should. That work also found the bounded-evaluation\nguard was not actually bounded: the wall clock is checked between\nmatches, and `(a+)+$` never returns from the first one. The old\nadversarial test passed because its sample was twenty characters and\nthe real adapter allows twenty thousand. A static guard now refuses the\ntwo shapes that explode, and twenty-three ordinary patterns are pinned\nas must-be-allowed so it cannot start crying wolf.\n\n225 files, 3472 tests, typecheck and lint clean.\n\n---\n\n四張合約一齊落地。\n\nCommand palette:一個快捷鍵通去所有嘢,30 行全部由現有 registry 砌出\n嚟 — 即係話隔籬加多個設定分頁,佢自己會出現,唔使等人記得。係設定\n嘅就直接俾你改,係去邊度嘅就講明去邊度。\n\n粒通知鐘本來得個殼,而家係真嘅通知中心。仲有兩個測試睇實份合約:一個\n證明四種通知都係角落彈出、成份文件冇 dialog、警告過一個鐘都仲喺度;\n另一個數齊全 package 每個 dialog,逐個要寫明「你要用家決定啲乜」—\n寫「我想話俾佢知」唔收貨。寫完當日就捉到隔籬啱啱加嘅 palette 😆\n\nChangelog 係由個 repo 度生出嚟,唔係人手寫:35 個版本 88 條記錄,每條\n掛住自己個 commit,寫之前逐個 SHA 驗過存唔存在。\n\nRegex builder 補返四個由頭到尾冇搜尋嘅清單,仲有個 profiles 名單。\n順手發現個「防爆」保護根本冇防到:計時器係兩次 match 之間先睇,而\n`(a+)+$` 第一次 match 就返唔到嚟。舊測試過到,係因為佢個樣本得二十\n個字,而真嘅適配器俾到二萬個。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface", "build", "docs", "shell"],
                files: 58,
            }
        ],
