                subject: "Bring the README up to date with what actually shipped",
                details: "It still said there were no releases, no installers, no download and no\ndocumentation site. All four are now wrong: every passing push publishes a real\nSquirrel installer, the site is live, and there are ten packages rather than\neight.\n\nAdds the screenshots, taken by the harness in CI from the real running app, with\nthe caveat that matters stated next to them: the world in those images is served\nby somebody else's BlueMap server, not rendered by this project, because the\nmesher does not exist yet. A reader who skims the pictures should not come away\nbelieving the thing works.\n\n個 README 仲寫住冇 release、冇 installer、冇得載、冇文件網站 — 四樣而家全部唔啱：\n每次 push 過關就出一個真 installer，個網站上咗線，package 由八個變十個。\n\n順手擺埋啲截圖上去，係 CI 入面影真 app 嘅。但一定要喺隔籬寫清楚：張相入面嗰個\n世界係人哋部 BlueMap server 畫嘅，唔係我哋畫嘅，因為 mesher 仲未寫。唔可以俾人\n掃兩眼張相就以為隻嘢已經做得晒。",
